,{"id":"1c18974f3a92","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.de_opificio","w":"bkv.cpg-3154","a":"gregor_v_nyssa","s":11,"p":[1,1],"r":[1,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Cf. Eccles. i. 8. The quotation is not from the LXX.: it is perhaps not intended to be verbal."},{"id":"dfb7a1ce8018","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_officiis","w":"ambrosius.de_officiis","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":3,"p":[1,1],"r":[3,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. iii. 7."},{"id":"3b551f6a1389","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_excessu_fratris","w":"ambrosius.de_excessu_fratris","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":2,"p":[29,29],"r":[4,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. iv. 2 ff."},{"id":"befb61ffb7dc","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_fide","w":"ambrosius.de_fide","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":41,"p":[6,6],"r":[12,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccl. xii. 14. Hurter observes that Goal would not judge rational creatures, were they not capable of advance or retrogression, of becoming better or falling into degradation, and had, as a matter of fact, advanced or fallen back."},{"id":"45d504e6488b","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_fide","w":"ambrosius.de_fide","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":79,"p":[10,10],"r":[12,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. xii. 14."},{"id":"b1cc900a3d5c","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_mysteriis","w":"ambrosius.de_mysteriis","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":1,"p":[43,43],"r":[2,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. ii. 14."},{"id":"3a937fab5ef7","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_paenitentia","w":"ambrosius.de_paenitentia","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":1,"p":[2,2],"r":[7,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. vii. 17."},{"id":"072f258c7740","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_paenitentia","w":"ambrosius.de_paenitentia","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":23,"p":[12,12],"r":[7,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. vii. 4."},{"id":"03f660b6e1f7","v":"npnf.ambrosius.epistulae","w":"ambrosius.epistulae","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":5,"p":[4,4],"r":[6,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Allusion is here made to a celebrated act of Valentinian, when attending on the Emperor Julian at the temple of Fortune. One of the attendants sprinkled him with lustral water, and Valentinian struck him with his fist, saying that this water defiled rather than purified those whom it touched. Comp. Sozomen, Hist. Eccl. VI. 6."},{"id":"b478f41963cd","v":"npnf.ambrosius.epistulae","w":"ambrosius.epistulae","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":5,"p":[10,10],"r":[7,13],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"A law in favour of the Arians, allowing them to meet together freely, passed through the influence of Justina. See Sozomen, Hist. Eccl. VII. 13."},{"id":"c5b6e306a340","v":"npnf.ambrosius.epistulae","w":"ambrosius.epistulae","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":9,"p":[15,15],"r":[3,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. iii. 1."},{"id":"d4782780010d","v":"npnf.ambrosius.epistulae","w":"ambrosius.epistulae","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":13,"p":[105,105],"r":[7,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccl. vii. 2."},{"id":"1a2951e8eb46","v":"lf.ambrosius.epistulae","w":"ambrosius.epistulae","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":3,"p":[6,6],"r":[11,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eccles. xi. 3."},{"id":"c7c3bb5d3a72","v":"lf.ambrosius.epistulae","w":"ambrosius.epistulae","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":14,"p":[3,3],"r":[5,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"a This Lucius was the person who, after the death of S. Athanasius, was forced upon the Church of Alexandria as Bishop, in the place of Peter who had been duly elected, by the Governor of the Province. His crimes and cruelties are recorded at length by Theodoret. Eccl. Hist. iv. 21, 22. He was eventually expe